planet-sim — third-party notices
=================================

planet-sim is the work of its authors; the engines, the physics, and the
visualization code are original. This file records the **one** piece of
third-party software the project *vendors* (carries a copy of), so that the
attribution its licence requires travels with the repository and with the
artifacts the repository emits.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
three.js  —  WebGL 3-D library  (revision r137, minified UMD build)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Homepage : https://threejs.org
  Source   : https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js  (tag r137)
  Vendored : planet/vendor/three.min.js  — the unmodified r137 minified UMD
             build, carried verbatim (its own `@license` banner left intact).
  Used by  : planet/flow_globe.py inlines this file into the self-contained
             HTML showcase it emits (docs/figures/planet-eddy-particles.html,
             the §9.5 "Rung C" particle flow-globe), so that the page opens
             straight off the filesystem (file://) with no network access — the
             reason it is vendored inline rather than loaded from a CDN.

  Only the three.js scene/camera/WebGL framework is vendored. The particle
  advection and the orbit camera control in planet/flow_globe.py are original
  (we build *on* three.js; we do not copy a particle or controls library).

